 emission of output for the specified duration according to the provided clock.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Delaying work using a custom clock is beneficial when you need precise control over timing behavior,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as testing with test clocks or synchronizing work with specific time sources."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Use this operator to implement retry backoff, throttling, or scheduled tasks that depend on a particular clock implementation."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Example","text":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let start = Date()","let clock = SuspendingClock()","let delayedTask = DeferredTask {","    \"Delayed with custom clock\"","}.delay(for: .seconds(1), clock: clock, tolerance: .milliseconds(100))","let result = try await delayedTask.execute()","let elapsed = Date().timeIntervalSince(start)","print(\"Result: \\(result) after \\(elapsed) seconds\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Availability: macOS 13.0, iOS 16.0, watchOS 9.0, tvOS 16.0, visionOS 1.0 and above.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"type":"text","text":") holds the one thread"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delay always waits out its whole duration, even when cancelled. A test clock is unaffected."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Delays the emission of output 